  "title": "Luke Skywalker's temptation",
  "section": "Movie Facts # 4 of 10",
  "description": "The filming of Return of the Jedi took place from January 11 to May 20, 1982 in Redwood National Park forests in California, the Yuma desert in Arizona, and at the Elstree Studios, United Kingdom. By all accounts it was a difficult shoot, even with producer/creator George Lucas mostly available to lend support. Unexpectedly, a serious wardrobe problem arose: all Imperial characters, regardless of rank, were presented wearing identical insignia (Imperial Navy Commander). No one on the film's production staff caught on to this error until halfway through shooting, and it remains uncorrected in the final version of Jedi."
